{{also|rúg|rüg}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{unc|en}}; probably of {{der|en|gmq|-}} origin; perhaps inherited via {{inh|en|enm|*rugge}} (suggested by {{m+|enm|ruggy|t=hairy, shaggy, bristly}} and {{m|enm|rugged|t=hairy, shaggy, rugged}}), from {{der|en|non|rǫgg|t=shagginess, tuft}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*rawwō||long wool}}, related to English {{m|en|rag}} and {{m|en|rough}}. Cognate with dialectal {{cog|no|rugga|t=coarse coverlet}}, {{cog|sv|rugg||rough entangled hair}}, related to {{m+|en|rag}} and {{m|en|rough}}. Compare also {{cog|ang|rȳhe|t=rug, rough covering, blanket}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|rŭg}}, {{IPA|en|/ɹʌɡ/}}
* {{audio|en|en-au-rug.ogg|Audio (AU)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʌɡ|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A partial covering for a floor. {{defdate|1624}}
